# Review ownership.
#
# Code owners are requested automatically on every pull request that touches a
# matching path. With a single maintainer this is mostly a record of who is
# expected to review what; it starts doing real work the moment a second
# maintainer is added.
#
# Syntax: <path pattern> <owner>...
# `@aijadugar` is a user, not a team. The repository is owned by a personal
# account (`aijadugar/skyboy`), so there is no organisation team to reference.

# Default: everything not matched below.
*                       @aijadugar

# Workflows and CI configuration. A change here can weaken every other check,
# so it should never be merged without the maintainer reading the diff.
/.github/               @aijadugar

# Dependency manifests: a dependency bump is a supply-chain change.
/package.json           @aijadugar
/package-lock.json      @aijadugar

# The website. Separate from the desktop app on purpose.
/apps/web/              @aijadugar
